{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-js","path":"/database-connection-pooling-concurrency/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<p>Under sudden traffic bursts, Node.js applications that create database connections on the fly can quickly exhaust PostgreSQL <code class=\"language-text\">max_connections</code>, leading to cascading gateway timeouts.</p>\n<p>Here are the best practices we used to keep database connections stable and resilient under heavy concurrent loads.</p>\n<h2 id=\"architecture--configuration\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#architecture--configuration\" aria-label=\"architecture  configuration permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Architecture &#x26; Configuration</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>PgBouncer in Transaction Pooling Mode</strong>:\nAllows thousands of client connections to share a small pool of 50–100 actual PostgreSQL backend processes.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Pool Tuning in Node.js</strong>:</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"javascript\"><pre class=\"language-javascript\"><code class=\"language-javascript\"><span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> Pool <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">require</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'pg'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> pool <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">Pool</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">host</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> process<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>env<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token constant\">DB_HOST</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">port</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token number\">5432</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">database</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> process<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>env<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token constant\">DB_NAME</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">user</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> process<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>env<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token constant\">DB_USER</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">password</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> process<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>env<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token constant\">DB_PASSWORD</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">max</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token number\">20</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// Max clients in local process pool</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">idleTimeoutMillis</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token number\">30000</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token literal-property property\">connectionTimeoutMillis</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token number\">2000</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span></code></pre></div>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li><strong>Circuit Breakers</strong>:\nImplementing graceful backoff and read-replica fallbacks when primary pool latency crosses established thresholds.</li>\n</ol>","excerpt":"Under sudden traffic bursts, Node.js applications that create database connections on the fly can quickly exhaust PostgreSQL , leading to…","tableOfContents":"<ul>\n<li><a href=\"#architecture--configuration\">Architecture &#x26; Configuration</a></li>\n</ul>","fields":{"slug":"/database-connection-pooling-concurrency/"},"frontmatter":{"title":"Database Connection Pooling and High-Concurrency Handling in Node.js","date":"July 14, 2023","dateISO":"2023-07-14","updatedISO":null,"tags":["postgresql","node","database","performance","backend"],"categories":["Engineering","Databases"],"description":"Configuring PgBouncer and node-postgres connection pools to prevent connection starvation under massive traffic spikes.","comments_off":null,"dated":null,"thumbnail":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","backgroundColor":"#080808","images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/07f5a193c5a1357203c0389b1002fb71/d431b/postgres.png","srcSet":"/static/07f5a193c5a1357203c0389b1002fb71/d431b/postgres.png 75w,\n/static/07f5a193c5a1357203c0389b1002fb71/60637/postgres.png 150w","sizes":"75px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/07f5a193c5a1357203c0389b1002fb71/d75d1/postgres.webp 75w,\n/static/07f5a193c5a1357203c0389b1002fb71/c970d/postgres.webp 150w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"75px"}]},"width":75,"height":75}}},"socialImage":{"childImageSharp":{"original":{"src":"/static/postgres-07f5a193c5a1357203c0389b1002fb71.png","width":960,"height":960}}}}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/database-connection-pooling-concurrency/","previous":{"id":"445243a8-1292-5c8c-bdda-cb08493db3cc","frontmatter":{"title":"High-Availability Cloud Migration to GCP: Compute Engine & Cloud SQL","tags":["gcp","cloud","devops","kubernetes","docker"],"categories":["Engineering","DevOps"],"template":"post","series":"Cloud Infrastructure & High Availability"},"fields":{"slug":"/gcp-high-availability-migration/"}},"next":{"id":"1c14d3e7-a6d0-5311-9c0f-706180d34cec","frontmatter":{"title":"Building Production RAG Pipelines with Node.js, LangChain & OpenAI","tags":["genai","rag","openai","node","langchain"],"categories":["Engineering","GenAI"],"template":"post","series":"Production GenAI & RAG Pipelines"},"fields":{"slug":"/building-rag-pipelines-with-langchain/"}}}},"staticQueryHashes":["924188448"],"slicesMap":{}}